Found in a bug hunt; reproduced and re-verified independently.

Cmd/Edit.pm:243,246,250,257,263,290,294; Cmd/Create.pm:172-176;
Cmd/Handoff.pm:136,141 guard their options on truth rather than
definedness/length, so the value "0" is indistinguishable from "not given".

The write still happens: the task ref is rewritten, `updated` is bumped by
BoardStore::save_task_cas, an activity-log entry is appended, and the
command prints "Updated task N: <old title>" and exits 0.

--body was converted to `defined ... && length` for ticket #78 in both edit
(line 248) and create (line 178); its siblings were not. The --append-body
case is self-contradicting -- its guard is `if ($self->append_body)` while
the comment immediately inside it reads "length, not truth: appending to a
body of "0" must not replace it (ticket #78)".

Reproduction:

    $ karr edit 1 --title 0
    Updated task 1: original title        exit=0
    $ karr edit 1 --block 0
    Updated task 1: original title        exit=0

    $ karr show 1 --json
    {... "title":"original title", ...}   # nothing landed, no `blocked`
                                          # but `updated` moved
    $ karr edit 1 --title 00              # works -- the giveaway that this
                                          # is truthiness, not validation

Same for create: `karr create "x" --tags 0 --assignee 0 --estimate 0`
records none of the three.

Cost: mostly narrow (a literal "0"), but --block 0 is the sharp edge -- karr
reports the card updated, the card is NOT blocked, and pick will hand it
straight out. Every case also writes a log entry and an `updated` bump for a
change that was discarded, so the audit trail records an edit that did not
happen.

kanban-md errors with "no changes specified" when an edit changes nothing
(internal/board/mutate.go:413-415); karr writes and reports success.

Fix: the #78 rule (`defined && length`) applied to the siblings, and
possibly a "no changes specified" refusal.
